module

public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.Coherent
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.CoherentAbelian.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjCoherentDegreeOne.GradedSections
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjSerreCorrespondence.IrrelevantModules
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjSerreCorrespondence.TwistedSectionsFunctor

/-!
# The quasi-inverse `ℱ ↦ ⨁_{n ≥ 0} Γ(X, ℱ(n))` lands in the finite graded modules

Let `A` be a graded ring whose degree-zero part `A₀` is Noetherian and which is generated by
finitely many elements of `A₁` over `A₀`, and let `X = Proj A`. Tags 0BXD and 0BXF name
`ℱ ↦ ⨁_{n ≥ 0} Γ(X, ℱ(n))` as the quasi-inverse of `M ↦ M̃`, which presupposes that the graded
`A`-module it produces from a *coherent* `ℱ` is finitely generated. That is assertion (4) of
[Stacks, Tag 0AG6] at `k = 0`, and this file reads it off:

`⨁_{n ≥ 0} Γ(X, ℱ(n))` is a finite `A`-module, so the construction is a functor

`Coh(𝒪_X) ⟶ Mod^fg_A`.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjSerreCorrespondence.nonnegTwistedSectionsFiniteObj`: the graded
  `A`-module `⨁_{n ≥ 0} Γ(X, ℱ(n))` of a coherent `ℱ`, as an object of `Mod^fg_A`.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjSerreCorrespondence.nonnegTwistedSectionsCoherentFunctor`: that
  construction as a functor `Coh(𝒪_X) ⟶ Mod^fg_A`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjSerreCorrespondence.moduleFinite_nonnegTwistedSections`:
  **`⨁_{n ≥ 0} Γ(X, ℱ(n))` is a finite `A`-module** for `ℱ` coherent.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjSerreCorrespondence.nonnegTwistedSectionsCoherentFunctor_obj` and
  `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjSerreCorrespondence.nonnegTwistedSectionsCoherentFunctor_map`: the
  functor is the construction just described, acting on morphisms by
  `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjSerreCorrespondence.nonnegTwistedSectionsMap`.

## Implementation notes

The two spellings of `⨁_{n ≥ 0} Γ(X, ℱ(n))` which meet here are **definitionally equal**, so no
transport is needed. `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjSerreCorrespondence`
`.nonnegTwistedSectionsSubmodule` is `Submodule.restrictScalars ℤ` of
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjTwistedSections.TwistedGlobalSectionsModule.truncation` at `k = 0`,
and restriction of scalars changes neither the carrier set nor the `A`-action — which is exactly
why `nonnegTwistedSectionsModule` can be obtained by `inferInstanceAs`. Hence
`Stacks.ProjCoherentDegreeOne.moduleFinite_truncation` at `k = 0` *is* the statement proved here,
and the proof is an application.

The generating family is carried in the unpadded form of
`Stacks.ProjCoherentDegreeOne.proj_isNoetherian_and_forall_isCoherent`, a family
`x : Fin n → A` of degree-one elements generating `A` over `A₀` with `n` arbitrary;
`Stacks.ProjCoherentDegreeOne.exists_two_le_generators` pads it to the `Fin (m + 1 + 1)` the
finiteness proof is stated at.

The grading index type `σ` lives in the universe of `A` rather than in an independent universe,
as it does throughout `StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/ProjCoherentDegreeOne/`; the comparison
machinery assertion (4) rests on is stated with both carriers and both index types in one
universe. So the objects here are those of `FiniteGradedModules.{u, u, u} 𝒜`, not of
`FiniteGradedModules.{u, u, w} 𝒜`.

Coherence is taken in the form `Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsCoherent`, the predicate
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.CoherentModules` is the full subcategory on, and converted to the
root-level `SheafOfModules.IsCoherent` that
`Stacks.ProjCoherentDegreeOne.moduleFinite_truncation` is stated with by
`AlgebraicGeometry.CoherentAbelian.isCoherent_of_stacksIsCoherent`. The library carries both
two-field classes; neither duplication nor its resolution belongs here.

**No `stacks` attribute.** This is one component of Tags 0BXD and 0BXF — the half of their
quasi-inverse clause saying that the quasi-inverse makes sense — and neither the equivalence nor
the quasi-inverse property is proved here. Nor is it a covering set for [Stacks, Tag 0AG6],
which is registered whole at
`Stacks.ProjCoherentDegreeOne.proj_isNoetherian_and_forall_isCoherent`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0AG6](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0AG6)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BXD](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BXD)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BXF](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BXF)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01BV](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01BV)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory Opposite TopologicalSpace
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjSheafFunctoriality (GradedModuleCat)
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjTwistFunctor (projRingSheaf)
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjTwistedSections (twistedGlobalSectionsModule)

namespace Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjSerreCorrespondence

universe u

attribute [local instance_reducible] ProjectiveSpectrum.top
attribute [local implicit_reducible] TopCat.Sheaf sheafCompose AlgebraicGeometry.Proj

variable {A : Type u} {σ : Type u} [CommRing A] [SetLike σ A] [AddSubgroupClass σ A]
  (𝒜 : ℕ → σ) [GradedRing 𝒜] [IsNoetherianRing (𝒜 0)] {n : ℕ} (x : Fin n → A)
  (hx : ∀ i, x i ∈ 𝒜 1) (hgen : Algebra.adjoin (𝒜 0) (Set.range x) = ⊤)

include hx hgen

/-- **`⨁_{n ≥ 0} Γ(X, ℱ(n))` is a finite `A`-module** for `ℱ` a coherent `𝒪_X`-module on
`X = Proj A`, when `A₀` is Noetherian and `A` is generated by finitely many elements of `A₁`
over `A₀`.

This is assertion (4) of [Stacks, Tag 0AG6] at `k = 0`: the degree-`≥ 0` truncation is
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjTwistedSections.TwistedGlobalSectionsModule.truncation` at `k = 0`
with its scalars restricted to `ℤ`, and restriction of scalars changes neither the carrier nor
the `A`-action. -/
theorem moduleFinite_nonnegTwistedSections (F : SheafOfModules.{u} (projRingSheaf 𝒜))
    (hF : Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsCoherent F) :
    letI := nonnegTwistedSectionsModule 𝒜 F
    Module.Finite A (nonnegTwistedSectionsSubmodule 𝒜 F) := by
  obtain ⟨m, y, hy, hygen⟩ := Stacks.ProjCoherentDegreeOne.exists_two_le_generators 𝒜 x hx hgen
  exact Stacks.ProjCoherentDegreeOne.moduleFinite_truncation 𝒜 F y hy hygen
    (AlgebraicGeometry.CoherentAbelian.isCoherent_of_stacksIsCoherent hF)
    (twistedGlobalSectionsModule 𝒜 F) 0

/-- **The graded `A`-module `⨁_{n ≥ 0} Γ(X, ℱ(n))` of a coherent `ℱ`, as an object of
`Mod^fg_A`**: the graded module of
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjSerreCorrespondence.nonnegTwistedSections` together with its
finite generation. -/
def nonnegTwistedSectionsFiniteObj (F : SheafOfModules.{u} (projRingSheaf 𝒜))
    (hF : Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsCoherent F) : FiniteGradedModules.{u, u, u} 𝒜 where
  obj := nonnegTwistedSections 𝒜 F
  property := moduleFinite_nonnegTwistedSections 𝒜 x hx hgen F hF

/-- **The quasi-inverse of Tags 0BXD and 0BXF as a functor `Coh(𝒪_X) ⟶ Mod^fg_A`**: a coherent
`𝒪_X`-module `ℱ` on `X = Proj A` goes to the finitely generated graded `A`-module
`⨁_{n ≥ 0} Γ(X, ℱ(n))`.

Functoriality is that of
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjSerreCorrespondence.nonnegTwistedSectionsFunctor`, restricted
along the inclusion of the coherent sheaves and lifted through the full subcategory of finitely
generated graded modules. This is not the equivalence of either tag, nor the assertion that it
is quasi-inverse to `M ↦ M̃`. -/
def nonnegTwistedSectionsCoherentFunctor :
    Stacks.SheafOfModules.CoherentModules (projRingSheaf 𝒜) ⥤ FiniteGradedModules.{u, u, u} 𝒜 :=
  ObjectProperty.lift (fun M : GradedModuleCat.{u, u, u} 𝒜 => Module.Finite A M.carrier)
    ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.coherentModules (projRingSheaf 𝒜)).ι ⋙
      nonnegTwistedSectionsFunctor 𝒜)
    fun F => moduleFinite_nonnegTwistedSections 𝒜 x hx hgen F.obj F.property

/-- The functor sends a coherent sheaf to `⨁_{n ≥ 0} Γ(X, ℱ(n))`, with its finite generation. -/
@[simp]
theorem nonnegTwistedSectionsCoherentFunctor_obj
    (F : Stacks.SheafOfModules.CoherentModules (projRingSheaf 𝒜)) :
    (nonnegTwistedSectionsCoherentFunctor 𝒜 x hx hgen).obj F =
      nonnegTwistedSectionsFiniteObj 𝒜 x hx hgen F.obj F.property :=
  rfl

/-- The functor sends a morphism of coherent sheaves to the induced morphism of graded
modules. -/
@[simp]
theorem nonnegTwistedSectionsCoherentFunctor_map
    {E F' : Stacks.SheafOfModules.CoherentModules (projRingSheaf 𝒜)} (φ : E ⟶ F') :
    ((nonnegTwistedSectionsCoherentFunctor 𝒜 x hx hgen).map φ).hom =
      nonnegTwistedSectionsMap 𝒜 φ.hom :=
  rfl

end Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjSerreCorrespondence

end
